WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.650
Wealth, fame, power...

3
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.440
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

4
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

5
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.360
attained this and everything else
the world had to offer.

6
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.820
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

7
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.660
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

8
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.660
You want my treasure?

9
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.700
You can have it!

10
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.450
Go ahead.

11
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.040
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

12
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.660
Find it!

13
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.250
Everything is right where I left it!

14
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.250
Now you just have to find it!

15
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.750
These words lured
men to the Grand Line

16
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.380
People set their sights on the Grand Line in pursuit of their dreams.

17
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.920
in pursuit of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine!

18
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.630
The world has truly entered the Great Pirate Era!

19
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.850
This is the time known as
the Great Pirate Era!

20
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.640
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

21
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.440
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

22
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.690
One Piece!

23
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.700
Compasses? Not for me. Left them all behind

24
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.500
I'm headed out to sea, with my heart serving as guide

25
00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.540
Following the ancient map to the spot marked "X" reveals

26
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.760
Yeah, it's only legendary till someone proves it's real

27
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.710
When the world's got you down,

28
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.850
lean on your crew, they'll turn it around

29
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.190
Their biorhythm will carry you through

30
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.230
We're gonna make the most of it

31
00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.400
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

32
00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.990
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

33
00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.040
Got some change to my name,

34
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.250
and maybe you wanna be my friend?

35
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.130
We are, we are on the cruise!

36
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.760
WE ARE!

37
00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:55.140
[KRIEG] So, you are alive.

38
00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:59.890
The unrivaled pirate captain
who was also the ship's cook.

39
00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:02.390
Yes, that's right, I'm still alive...

40
00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:05.480
But what has any of this
got to do with you?

41
00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:08.020
I haven't been a pirate
for many years now.

42
00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.070
I chose the life of a cook.

43
00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:12.900
[laughs]

44
00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.620
"Chose the life of a cook," huh?

45
00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:17.120
Yeah, right.

46
00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.040
You didn't have a choice, old man.

47
00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:23.000
You live as a cook because the only
thing you can be now is a cook.

48
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.000
He was known far and wide...

49
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:30.920
Red Foot Zeff was a master of deadly
kicks who never used his hands in battle.

50
00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:34.430
It was said that with his mighty legs,
he could crush bedrock to sand,

51
00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:37.970
and leave footprints on solid steel.

52
00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:41.220
"Red Foot" referred to his
boots which became soaked

53
00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:46.690
in the blood of his enemies
as he kicked them down.

54
00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:52.440
You know, it really is a pity that you no
longer have that precious leg of yours.

55
00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:55.990
I heard that rumor some time ago.

56
00:02:55.990 --> 00:03:00.080
How unlucky for you to have
such an accident at sea.

57
00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:03.250
Now that your greatest weapon
has been sacrificed to the sea,

58
00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:06.580
you're defenseless,
completely unable to fight.

59
00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:08.920
[ZEFF] I don't need to fight anymore.

60
00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:09.960
I'm a cook.

61
00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:13.670
And as long as I have my two
hands for that, I'll be just fine.

62
00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.680
Enough chitchat,
let's get to the point.

63
00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.470
What do you want from me?

64
00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:18.850
[KRIEG chuckles]

65
00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:20.760
Red... Foot...

66
00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:22.680
You're the man who
sailed the perilous waters

67
00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:25.270
of the Grand Line and
came back unscathed...

68
00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:26.480
Impressive.

69
00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:29.690
There should be a logbook
detailing your tactics,

70
00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:32.570
a full year of your journey there...

71
00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:34.240
Give it to me... now!

72
00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.700
[ZEFF grunts]

73
00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:37.700
Whoa! So is he sayin'

74
00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:40.160
you've been to the
Grand Line too, Pops?

75
00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.530
Yeah.

76
00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:43.660
My logbook, huh?

77
00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:47.620
You're right, I do indeed
have a record of my travels.

78
00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:50.080
But I will never hand it over to you.

79
00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:51.250
[KRIEG] Huh?

80
00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:55.050
You ignorant brute...
That logbook is sacred to me.

81
00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:58.180
It's the pride of the
crewmen that I sailed with.

82
00:03:58.180 --> 00:04:01.720
It's far too important to give to you.

83
00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:04.720
All right... I'll take it.

84
00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.980
Yes... It's true that
the Grand Line beat me.

85
00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.650
Still... I will never give up on it!

86
00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.980
I am Don Krieg!

87
00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:15.650
In the end, it's just another ocean.

88
00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:19.660
I had enough weapons...
and men... and ambition!

89
00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:24.700
[KRIEG] Regrettably, the only
thing I lacked was information.

90
00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:28.120
I just didn't know enough.

91
00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:31.580
But now, I'll fix all that.

92
00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:34.550
Once I have your logbook,
I'll form another pirate fleet

93
00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:37.220
and seize the legendary One Piece.

94
00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:41.140
Then, I will stand as ruler
of this great pirate era!

95
00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:46.140
<b>The Oath</b>

96
00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.230
[LUFFY] Now, hold on!

97
00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:50.600
It's me who's gonna be
King of the Pirates!

98
00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.270
– [COOKS gasp]
– [COOK U] Chore Boy?

99
00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.650
Wait! Don't be such an idiot!

100
00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:57.900
You better back off, Chore Boy!

101
00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:02.530
No way, not from this.

102
00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:05.160
Did you say something, kid?

103
00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:08.000
I won't allow that kind
of stupidity again.

104
00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.080
Oh yeah, well, stupid or not...

105
00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.790
I'm just stating the
facts like they are.

106
00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:15.000
This isn't a game.

107
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.460
Yeah, I know...

108
00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:18.970
I'm still gonna conquer the Grand Line.

109
00:05:18.970 --> 00:05:21.430
[KRIEG growls]
No, you won't!

110
00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:24.260
It's true that we didn't have
the information we needed;

111
00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:28.770
but my fleet of five thousand men was
wiped out in just seven days, you brat!

112
00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:30.060
That sea is hell!

113
00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:32.060
What?! One week?!

114
00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:35.610
Don Krieg's ships were
wiped out in seven days?!

115
00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:37.280
[COOK KK] What happened out there?

116
00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:42.530
Unfortunately, I don't find your
smart-assed remarks very amusing.

117
00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:47.910
If you insist on this foolish behavior,
I'll crush you right here and right now.

118
00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.870
Go ahead, if you can.

119
00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:52.250
[KRIEG growls]

120
00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:54.040
[KRIEG] I can, and I will.

121
00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:58.380
It would be my pleasure to send you
to an early grave, you cocky runt.

122
00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:06.930
What's going on, Luffy?
You need a hand?

123
00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:09.890
If you don't need help,
that's okay, too!

124
00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:12.890
Oh, hey, guys. Appreciate the offer...

125
00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:14.980
But I think I can handle this clown.

126
00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:16.520
Aw, too bad!

127
00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:21.110
Are those two guys your "crew"?

128
00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:24.160
That's a pretty small
group you got there, kid.

129
00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:25.240
Well, that's not all...

130
00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:26.410
I got two more!

131
00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:29.410
I'm not a part of your crew!

132
00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:30.450
[KRIEG growls]

133
00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:32.790
[KRIEG] I'll deal with you later.

134
00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:35.330
Right now, I'm going to go feed my men.

135
00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:40.590
Those of you who don't wish to die,

136
00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:45.180
can leave the restaurant
now and escape that fate.

137
00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:48.350
The only things I'm after are
the logbook and this ship.

138
00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:54.060
[KRIEG] However, if you wish
to stay and be slaughtered...

139
00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:58.360
I have no problem burying every
last one of you at sea...

140
00:06:58.360 --> 00:06:59.980
Know that.

141
00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:06.740
[GHIN groaning]
I'm... so sorry, Sanji...

142
00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:09.580
I never thought it would be this way.

143
00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:13.040
[ZEFF] You have nothing
to apologize for, sailor.

144
00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:14.580
[PATTY gasps]

145
00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:18.920
[ZEFF] Every cook at this restaurant
did what they thought was right.

146
00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:21.000
That's all there is to say about that.

147
00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.380
But, Boss!

148
00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:25.550
Why are you acting as if
you're taking Sanji's side?!

149
00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:27.300
This mess is his fault!

150
00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:28.300
[COOK V] He's right!

151
00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:30.680
Sanji is responsible for
this whole damn thing!

152
00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:33.350
Yeah, Boss! That man's gonna
put your precious restaurant

153
00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:35.140
out of business!

154
00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:37.770
You fools don't know what
you're talking about!

155
00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:42.780
None of you have any idea what it's
like to be on the brink of starvation...

156
00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:46.150
To have no food or water
on the open ocean...

157
00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:51.280
There is no way you could possibly understand
what a terrifying prospect that is!

158
00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:54.540
It's the most difficult
situation a man can ever face!

159
00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:55.410
What?

160
00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:58.040
I don't know what you're
talkin' about, Chef Zeff.

161
00:07:58.040 --> 00:08:01.040
[ZEFF] If all you're gonna
do is stand around grumbling,

162
00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:02.550
– then leave this place
– [COOKS gasp]

163
00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:03.920
and never come back.

164
00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:08.300
[PATTY] I, for one,
am gonna stay and fight!

165
00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:11.470
I couldn't live with myself
if I accepted defeat!

166
00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:12.810
[COOK W] I'm staying, too!

167
00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:15.430
After all, this is our
restaurant, isn't it?!

168
00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:18.350
That's right, and this place
is all I've got, too!

169
00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:20.770
What are you doing?!

170
00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:24.440
You saw how powerful Don is, right?!

171
00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:26.150
[SANJI] Hey, Ghin!

172
00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:28.820
Listen up because I'm only
going to say this once.

173
00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:33.080
Feeding someone who's hungry
is my sacred moral duty.

174
00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:33.870
But...

175
00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:42.590
Now that your crew is well fed,
I have no obligation to them.

176
00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:47.130
With a clean conscience, I can beat
every last one of them to a bloody pulp.

177
00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:50.300
If anyone tries to take the
restaurant... they're dead.

178
00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:53.260
I'll kill them without a
moment's hesitation.

179
00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:55.010
Got that?

180
00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:56.770
[GHIN gulps]

181
00:08:56.770 --> 00:08:59.190
[PATTY] Hah! You're a real
head-case, Sanji.

182
00:08:59.190 --> 00:09:01.650
Letting him live, then
threatening to kill him?

183
00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:03.440
Can it, cook.

184
00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:05.690
[LUFFY] See? This guy's awesome, huh?

185
00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:08.110
Who cares how awesome he is?!

186
00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:10.030
We gotta get out of here right now!

187
00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:11.570
Easy there, Luffy...

188
00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:14.450
It is Don Krieg, but he's
in pretty sad shape.

189
00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:16.620
[LUFFY] Hm. Hey, Ghin!

190
00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:19.000
You said you didn't know
anything about the Grand Line...

191
00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:20.620
But I thought you'd been there.

192
00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:22.210
That doesn't make any sense...

193
00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:25.670
Nothing makes any sense now.

194
00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:30.340
What happened to us on the seventh day
of our journey through that cursed sea...

195
00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:34.600
I don't know if it was
a dream... or reality.

196
00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:37.850
I saw things that I can't
bring myself to believe.

197
00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:46.400
I know in my heart that it's impossible...
for that entire fifty-ship fleet...

198
00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:51.490
... to be completely
eradicated by a single man.

199
00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:53.200
[COOKS gasp, whimper]

200
00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:55.490
[USOPP screams]

201
00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:57.580
[LUFFY gasps]

202
00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:59.040
[COOKS] What?!

203
00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:05.250
[GHIN] It all happened so fast...

204
00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:07.460
As soon as this man appeared,

205
00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:11.090
he began to systematically sink
our ships one after another.

206
00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:17.600
[GHIN] If that raging storm
hadn't come upon us when it did,

207
00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:20.770
then that monster would have
destroyed our flagship as well.

208
00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:33.360
[GHIN] I don't know if a
single other ship made it out.

209
00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:37.830
It all seems like a terrible
nightmare burned into my memory!

210
00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:40.160
I just want to forget!

211
00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.950
His eyes...

212
00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:46.330
They were like a hawk's,
sharp and murderous.

213
00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:49.800
His gaze alone felt like
the cold hand of death!

214
00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:50.800
[ZORO gasps]

215
00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:50.800
[USOPP] Huh?

216
00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:55.090
[ZORO] What did he just say?!

217
00:10:56.470 --> 00:10:58.180
[GHIN growling]

218
00:10:58.180 --> 00:11:00.680
[ZEFF] Well then...

219
00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:02.310
That can only be the one

220
00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:05.440
– known as Hawk-Eye.
– [COOK B] What?

221
00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:07.980
[ZEFF] Your description
of his heartless gaze

222
00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:11.360
isn't proof of his identity
in and of itself...

223
00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:14.400
But the way he so easily
decimated your fleet

224
00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:17.950
confirms without a
doubt, that it's him.

225
00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:20.580
Hawk-Eye Mihawk.

226
00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:23.410
So you know him, Zoro?

227
00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:25.040
Yeah, I do...

228
00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:27.330
He's the man I've been looking for.

229
00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:33.630
[SANJI] Could that man have had some
kind of score to settle with you guys?

230
00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:35.220
[GHIN] We didn't do anything to him!

231
00:11:35.220 --> 00:11:38.010
[ZEFF] Perhaps you
disturbed him during a nap.

232
00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:39.090
Stupid cook!

233
00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:43.390
Why would he destroy an entire
fleet for something so trivial?!

234
00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:46.140
[ZEFF chuckles]
There's no reason to shout...

235
00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:48.520
It's just an example.

236
00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:50.610
I thought you might like
a little friendly advice

237
00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:53.820
on what kind of a place
the Grand Line is.

238
00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:56.450
And what kind of place is that?

239
00:11:56.450 --> 00:11:59.200
He probably means that
anything can happen there.

240
00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:00.370
[USOPP sobs]

241
00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:04.080
Hey, Luffy! Do we really,
really have to go there?

242
00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:05.250
Luffy?

243
00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:07.580
[ZORO, USOPP] Hm?

244
00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:10.880
[USOPP] Hey... Luffy...?

245
00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:13.920
[LUFFY laughs]
That's so awesome!

246
00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:15.970
This is gonna be such a blast!

247
00:12:15.970 --> 00:12:19.340
Don't you understand
the concept of "danger"?!

248
00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:23.680
[ZORO] Finally, my life's goal will
be achieved on the Grand Line.

249
00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:25.020
What...?!

250
00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:26.770
My rival...

251
00:12:26.770 --> 00:12:29.600
He's out there somewhere,
and I'm gonna find him.

252
00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:34.020
[SANJI] Are you that stupid?

253
00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:36.610
It's idiots like you
guys that end up dead.

254
00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:39.410
[ZORO] That may be true...

255
00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:41.570
But lay off the name-calling.

256
00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:46.910
I devoted my entire life to becoming
the world's greatest swordsman.

257
00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:51.130
I made my choice, so I'm the only
one who gets to call me stupid.

258
00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:55.630
Hey! What about me?!

259
00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:58.380
Me too, right?! I mean,
it only seems fair.

260
00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:00.090
Shut up, stupid.

261
00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.430
[SANJI sighs]
What morons.

262
00:13:07.730 --> 00:13:09.730
[PATTY] Enough!

263
00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:13.730
Do any of you maggots understand
the current situation?!

264
00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:16.820
That enormous galleon moored
in front of our dear little

265
00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:20.950
restaurant is none other
than Don Krieg's flagship!

266
00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:24.660
So why don't we check back into
reality and deal with this?!

267
00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:27.620
[PIRATE B] What the hell are you?!

268
00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:36.550
[PIRATES cheering]
Yeah! We're saved!

269
00:13:36.550 --> 00:13:39.170
[PIRATE A] I can't
believe it! We're alive!

270
00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:40.550
[PIRATE B] It's like a dream!

271
00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:42.010
[PIRATE C] Nightmare's finally over!

272
00:13:42.010 --> 00:13:45.550
[PIRATE D] We sailed into the pirate
graveyard, but we came back alive!

273
00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:52.020
That's right... And I'm
glad you all made it

274
00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:55.560
because I'll need a healthy crew
to go back to the Grand Line.

275
00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:58.230
[PIRATES gasp]

276
00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:01.570
Hey... Why the long faces?

277
00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:05.200
Sir... Why are we going back there?

278
00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:06.370
[gunshot]

279
00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:13.580
Point taken... Are there
any other objections?

280
00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:15.830
[PIRATES] Uhh...

281
00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:18.840
[PIRATES cheer]

282
00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:28.470
[KRIEG] First, we need to take
over that floating restaurant.

283
00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:32.520
Then, we can abandon the wreck
we're on before it falls apart.

284
00:14:32.520 --> 00:14:36.520
Don't worry about the enemy;
they're just a bunch of prissy cooks.

285
00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:38.270
It won't take much to crush them.

286
00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:49.370
– Attack!
– [PIRATES yell]

287
00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:53.710
Hear that?! They're gonna be here soon!

288
00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:54.920
[COOK C] The restaurant is ours!

289
00:14:54.920 --> 00:14:57.750
And I'll fight to the
death to keep it that way!

290
00:15:21.070 --> 00:15:23.360
What's going on?!

291
00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:27.410
[PIRATE LL] The main ship... It was cut!

292
00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:32.330
It was cut?! What do you mean "cut"?!

293
00:15:32.330 --> 00:15:34.460
Something sliced up this galleon?

294
00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:37.370
No way... It can't be!

295
00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:40.210
That's impossible!

296
00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:43.960
[COOKS gasp, scream]

297
00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:46.090
Raise the anchor!

298
00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:47.970
Or we'll sink along with them!

299
00:15:47.970 --> 00:15:49.970
[COOK H] Yes, sir!

300
00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:51.180
[LUFFY grunts]

301
00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:54.180
Wait... Nami and the guys are
still on our ship out there!

302
00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:57.020
[USOPP gasps]

303
00:15:57.020 --> 00:15:59.770
[USOPP groans]
I hope it's not too late!

304
00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:01.690
[LUFFY pants, gasps]

305
00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:05.940
[LUFFY gasps]

306
00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:07.860
[USOPP screams]

307
00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:09.950
Hey! Big Bro!

308
00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:11.240
[YOSAKU] Big Bro!

309
00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:13.290
[LUFFY] Yosaku! Johnny!

310
00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:15.410
[LUFFY] Are you okay?!

311
00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:16.830
[ZORO] What happened to the ship?!

312
00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:18.540
Where's Nami? Is she okay?

313
00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:20.040
[YOSAKU] I'm sorry, Big Bro...!

314
00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:23.460
I don't know how to say
this, but... she's gone!

315
00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:26.510
[NAMI] See ya! Oh, and
make sure to tell them...

316
00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:28.300
Big Sis Nami!

317
00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:30.930
[NAMI] If it's meant to be,
I'll see them real soon!

318
00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:34.890
She took all the treasure
and sailed away!

319
00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:36.100
[ALL gasp]

320
00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:38.230
[ALL] She did what?!

321
00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:50.490
[ZEFF gasps]

322
00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:52.160
That man is...

323
00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:09.380
[LUFFY gasps]

324
00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:10.470
What'd you say?!

325
00:17:10.470 --> 00:17:13.470
For real?! Nami sailed off
with the Going Merry?!

326
00:17:13.470 --> 00:17:16.390
I need a straight answer!
Now, what happened?!

327
00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:25.110
Well... It all happened
in only a few minutes.

328
00:17:29.240 --> 00:17:31.490
[YOSAKU] Hey, what's the matter, Big Sis?

329
00:17:31.490 --> 00:17:32.570
Huh?

330
00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:35.370
Say, I don't really mean to pry or
anything, but whatcha looking at?

331
00:17:35.370 --> 00:17:37.200
Oh well, it's nothing really.

332
00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:40.620
Nice! Now that's a big bounty pirate...

333
00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:42.580
I gotta say, I'm impressed.

334
00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:44.080
But Big Sis...

335
00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:46.460
I think you're aiming a little
too high going after Arlong.

336
00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:49.050
I'm not kidding, that
guy's really bad news.

337
00:17:49.050 --> 00:17:51.340
He was playing it cool and
laying low for a while...

338
00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:52.800
You know, staying out of sight.

339
00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:56.220
[YOSAKU] But these days,
that maniac is causing all sorts of trouble.

340
00:17:56.220 --> 00:18:00.100
It's kinda tough walking away from
a twenty million berry bounty though.

341
00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:02.060
[JOHNNY] That guy is so
powerful that there is the

342
00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:06.520
slightest, tiniest chance that
we could lose and, well, die...

343
00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:07.190
[JOHNNY, YOSAKU] Uh...

344
00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:10.030
[YOSAKU] Big Sis Nami?

345
00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:12.030
Hey, would you guys mind turning around

346
00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:15.280
while I change into
something more comfortable?

347
00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:16.830
Yeah, sure... I don't mind.

348
00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:18.790
Changing? Like right now?

349
00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:20.200
It's so hot...

350
00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:22.790
[YOSAKU, JOHNNY gasp]
Yeah, you're hot... Uh, it's hot!

351
00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:30.760
Have you ever met a
woman who's that daring?

352
00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:33.680
Hey, what do you say we turn
around and see if she's done yet?

353
00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:34.890
[JOHNNY] Good idea!

354
00:18:34.890 --> 00:18:37.220
[BOTH gasp, scream]

355
00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:43.600
What the hell do you
think you're doing?!

356
00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:46.440
I'm doing business, of course!

357
00:18:46.440 --> 00:18:49.070
Use your heads, guys. I'm a
thief who only targets pirates

358
00:18:49.070 --> 00:18:51.030
and my next score is this ship.

359
00:18:51.030 --> 00:18:53.650
I never said anything about
being a member of this crew,

360
00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:56.160
I was just traveling
with them, nothing more.

361
00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:58.780
Even though I only spent a short
time with Luffy and the gang,

362
00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:01.750
I sure had a lot of fun...

363
00:19:01.750 --> 00:19:03.410
Make sure to tell them that I said...

364
00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:04.410
[JOHNNY, YOSAKU] Huh?

365
00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:08.540
If it's truly meant to be,
I'll see them real soon.

366
00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:11.800
Hey! Where are you going?!

367
00:19:11.800 --> 00:19:12.960
[YOSAKU, JOHNNY scream]

368
00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:17.840
[YOSAKU, JOHNNY gasp]

369
00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:19.850
We're gonna be in so much trouble!

370
00:19:19.850 --> 00:19:25.060
Our only job was to look after the ship,
and you're making us fail miserably!

371
00:19:30.400 --> 00:19:33.740
So that's the story of how
Big Sis Nami took the ship!

372
00:19:33.740 --> 00:19:34.570
Sorry!

373
00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:35.400
[ZORO grunts]

374
00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:38.780
Dammit! She just had to
make a bad situation worse!

375
00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:41.120
The heartless thief!
Kaya gave us that ship!

376
00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:43.080
[LUFFY] Wait! I see a ship!

377
00:19:43.080 --> 00:19:45.410
It's the Going Merry!

378
00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:46.870
Tell me where your boat is!

379
00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:49.000
We have it moored to the restaurant!

380
00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:50.960
Zoro! Usopp! Don't just stand there!

381
00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:52.800
Take their ship and go get Nami!

382
00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:54.880
Calm down... Let her keep the ship.

383
00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:58.140
Trust me, that woman is way
more trouble than she's worth.

384
00:19:58.140 --> 00:20:01.260
She's the only person I'll
accept as the ship's navigator!

385
00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:04.520
Fine, I'll do it...

386
00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:07.520
You're one high-maintenance
captain, you know that?

387
00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:08.980
All right, Usopp, let's go!

388
00:20:08.980 --> 00:20:10.230
[USOPP] Uh, okay!

389
00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:15.400
[JOHNNY, YOSAKU] The ship's
ready for action, Big Bro Zoro!

390
00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:16.570
Hey, what about you?

391
00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:18.240
I should probably
stick around here till

392
00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:19.910
I get this thing settled
with the restaurant.

393
00:20:19.910 --> 00:20:20.820
Know what I mean?

394
00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:21.910
Well, be careful...

395
00:20:21.910 --> 00:20:24.790
The situation here could
get really bad really fast.

396
00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:26.580
Yeah... Got that right.

397
00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:28.620
[PIRATE B] The ship has
been broken to splinters!

398
00:20:29.750 --> 00:20:31.710
Over there! It's that man!

399
00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:33.550
[gasps] He came back!

400
00:20:33.550 --> 00:20:35.550
[PIRATE OO gasping]

401
00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:39.970
[PIRATE A] Don Krieg!

402
00:20:39.970 --> 00:20:42.640
The man who destroyed
our fleet is back!

403
00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:43.640
What are we gonna do?!

404
00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:44.640
[group gasp]

405
00:20:48.060 --> 00:20:50.310
That's... That's him...

406
00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:55.610
– [heartbeat thumps]
– [ZORO gulps]

407
00:20:55.610 --> 00:20:59.650
[thumping continues]

408
00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:01.360
That man is...

409
00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:05.660
[KRIEG] That son of a bitch...

410
00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:10.460
That psycho followed us back
here! He's gonna kill us all!

411
00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:13.080
Everybody's gonna die!

412
00:21:13.080 --> 00:21:14.840
Hey...

413
00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:16.920
Who's that?

414
00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:19.930
[ZORO] That's the man
I've been looking for...

415
00:21:19.930 --> 00:21:22.760
Hawk-Eye Mihawk.

416
00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:25.010
So that's Mihawk.

417
00:21:25.060 --> 00:21:29.980
<b>"Hawk Eye" Mihawk
The Greatest Swordsman
in the World</b>

418
00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:33.360
Yeah... The greatest swordsman.

419
00:21:35.320 --> 00:21:38.070
That's gotta be the guy
who destroyed Krieg's fleet!

420
00:21:38.070 --> 00:21:41.910
He sunk fifty pirate ships out on
the Grand Line all by himself!

421
00:21:41.910 --> 00:21:45.620
Looks like he came back to finish
the job, but is that all he wants?

422
00:21:45.620 --> 00:21:49.410
Wait a minute... He just
looks like any ordinary man.

423
00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:53.040
He doesn't even appear to have any
kind of special weapons with him.

424
00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:54.920
He carries his weapon on his back.

425
00:21:54.920 --> 00:21:57.340
[PATTY] That's impossible!

426
00:21:57.340 --> 00:22:01.720
[CARNE] He couldn't have destroyed a galleon
like that using nothing but a sword!

427
00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:04.850
Hawk-Eye Mihawk... is a true master.

428
00:22:04.850 --> 00:22:08.680
He is without a doubt the
greatest swordsman in the world.

429
00:22:13.270 --> 00:22:15.270
[PIRATE SS] You... You monster!

430
00:22:15.270 --> 00:22:16.690
Why are you doing this to us?!

431
00:22:16.690 --> 00:22:18.780
What the hell have we
ever done to you?!

432
00:22:20.110 --> 00:22:21.570
[MIHAWK] Just killing time.

433
00:22:21.570 --> 00:22:22.700
[PIRATE SS growls]

434
00:22:22.700 --> 00:22:24.240
Bastard!

435
00:22:33.210 --> 00:22:34.960
[PIRATES gasp]

436
00:22:34.960 --> 00:22:36.210
What?! I missed?!

437
00:22:36.210 --> 00:22:38.380
But I aimed straight for him!

438
00:22:38.380 --> 00:22:39.500
He diverted them.

439
00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:40.340
[PIRATE SS gasps]

440
00:22:40.340 --> 00:22:44.180
He changed the course of the bullets
using the tip of his sword.

441
00:22:44.180 --> 00:22:45.550
[PIRATE SS] That can't be!

442
00:22:46.720 --> 00:22:49.430
Hold on! Who do you think you are?!

443
00:22:49.430 --> 00:22:53.810
I've never see a sword handled
so gently, or with such grace.

444
00:22:53.810 --> 00:22:57.230
There's no strength in
swordplay based on force.

445
00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:00.190
[ZORO] Did you also use that
sword to slice up this ship?

446
00:23:00.190 --> 00:23:01.650
[MIHAWK] I did.

447
00:23:01.650 --> 00:23:03.400
Then it's true...

448
00:23:03.400 --> 00:23:04.910
You're the best.

449
00:23:04.910 --> 00:23:07.410
He's got three swords!
It couldn't be...!

450
00:23:07.410 --> 00:23:11.160
I set sail for only one
reason... to meet you.

451
00:23:11.160 --> 00:23:12.830
And what is your goal?

452
00:23:12.830 --> 00:23:13.960
To beat you.

453
00:23:13.960 --> 00:23:15.170
[MIHAWK chuckles]

454
00:23:15.170 --> 00:23:16.330
How foolish...

455
00:23:34.350 --> 00:23:36.310
They sure were nice guys.

456
00:23:36.310 --> 00:23:37.810
But, I wonder...

457
00:23:37.810 --> 00:23:39.110
Well...

458
00:23:39.110 --> 00:23:41.940
I wonder if they would
let me join them again?

459
00:23:41.940 --> 00:23:44.650
I hope I see them.

460
00:23:45.240 --> 00:23:48.820
Free. I just wanna be free.

461
00:23:51.120 --> 00:23:52.990
I'm sorry, Bell-mère.

462
00:23:57.080 --> 00:24:00.290
You've got spare time,
so let's do this.

463
00:24:00.290 --> 00:24:03.420
Whoa! No way! It's him! Roronoa Zoro!

464
00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:05.300
It's Zoro of the Three-Swords Style!

465
00:24:05.300 --> 00:24:06.630
It is?!

466
00:24:06.630 --> 00:24:09.260
Really? A pirate hunter?

467
00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:11.680
He's a what?!

468
00:24:14.470 --> 00:24:16.350
Hey Luffy, we'd better hurry! Come on!

469
00:24:16.350 --> 00:24:19.350
The Going Merry is about
to sail right out of sight!

470
00:24:19.350 --> 00:24:21.270
Hey! Luffy!

471
00:24:21.270 --> 00:24:22.570
A fight...

472
00:24:23.690 --> 00:24:26.070
You're a weak, pitiful creature.

473
00:24:30.530 --> 00:24:32.620
[MIHAWK] If you are in fact
a competent swordsman,

474
00:24:32.620 --> 00:24:36.750
you should see the disparity in our
abilities, even before we cross swords.

475
00:24:37.790 --> 00:24:40.670
I must ask you why have
you challenged me?

476
00:24:40.670 --> 00:24:44.500
Could it be your courage?
Or is it simply your ignorance?

477
00:24:44.500 --> 00:24:46.760
My ambition drives me!

478
00:24:49.380 --> 00:24:52.680
Also... I made a promise
I intend to keep.

479
00:24:52.680 --> 00:24:56.310
The greatest swordsman in the world
going up against Roronoa Zoro...

480
00:24:56.310 --> 00:24:58.060
Two masters of swordplay...

481
00:24:58.060 --> 00:25:00.650
What kind of a fight is
this gonna turn out to be?

482
00:25:00.650 --> 00:25:04.400
There isn't a person alive
who can defeat Big Bro.

483
00:25:04.400 --> 00:25:06.860
He's already the best in the world!

484
00:25:08.610 --> 00:25:09.610
[ZORO gasps]

485
00:25:11.110 --> 00:25:14.450
Funny... What do you think
you're gonna do with that?

486
00:25:14.450 --> 00:25:15.660
It'll be more than adequate.

487
00:25:15.660 --> 00:25:18.960
After all, you wouldn't kill
a fly with a cannon, would you?

488
00:25:18.960 --> 00:25:22.170
You may have quite the
reputation on the East Blue,

489
00:25:22.170 --> 00:25:24.500
but that doesn't mean much to me.

490
00:25:24.500 --> 00:25:28.380
This sea is by far
the weakest of the four.

491
00:25:28.380 --> 00:25:32.260
Unfortunately, I don't carry any
blades smaller than this one.

492
00:25:32.260 --> 00:25:35.810
I have had just about
enough of your attitude.

493
00:25:36.390 --> 00:25:38.100
[ZORO] Now, you die!

494
00:25:38.100 --> 00:25:41.560
You have no idea how
big the world really is.

495
00:25:41.560 --> 00:25:43.350
[ZORO] Oni Giri!

496
00:25:50.950 --> 00:25:52.200
[ZORO gasps] What the...?!

497
00:25:53.740 --> 00:25:55.450
Zoro!

498
00:25:55.450 --> 00:25:58.580
What?! Big Bro's Oni Giri was stopped?!

499
00:25:58.580 --> 00:26:02.040
But that's crazy! That attack
never fails to stop an enemy!

500
00:26:02.040 --> 00:26:04.330
What's going on here?!

501
00:26:04.330 --> 00:26:08.250
[ZORO] I can't move my swords!
What has he done?!

502
00:26:08.250 --> 00:26:11.010
No one's been able to defend
against that technique...

503
00:26:11.010 --> 00:26:13.470
He stopped it with a pocketknife!

504
00:26:13.470 --> 00:26:16.640
No... Th... This can't be happening!

505
00:26:16.640 --> 00:26:19.060
He can't be this much better than me!

506
00:26:19.060 --> 00:26:22.060
There's no way our skills
are this far apart!

507
00:26:23.270 --> 00:26:27.190
[ZORO yells] I'm not that far
behind the world's strongest!

508
00:26:27.190 --> 00:26:29.480
[ZORO grunting]

509
00:26:29.480 --> 00:26:31.490
[YOSAKU, JOHNNY whimpering]

510
00:26:31.490 --> 00:26:32.700
[ZORO groans]

511
00:26:32.700 --> 00:26:33.910
[ZORO grunts]

512
00:26:33.910 --> 00:26:35.120
[YOSAKU, JOHNNY gasp]

513
00:26:35.120 --> 00:26:37.620
You're just toying with him,
right?! Fight for real, Big Bro!

514
00:26:37.620 --> 00:26:39.330
Big Bro!

515
00:26:39.330 --> 00:26:42.080
You can't be that much better than me!

516
00:26:43.830 --> 00:26:46.380
[ZORO yells]

517
00:26:56.050 --> 00:26:58.140
Such ferocious swordplay.

518
00:26:58.140 --> 00:26:59.430
[ZORO yells]

519
00:27:05.230 --> 00:27:09.070
[PIRATE SS] How can he defend against Zoro's
Three-Sword Style with such a small knife?!

520
00:27:09.070 --> 00:27:12.440
[PIRATE VV] He's more of a monster
with a blade than even the great Zoro!

521
00:27:12.440 --> 00:27:15.610
[ZORO] I did not devote my
entire life to swordsmanship...

522
00:27:15.610 --> 00:27:18.700
to be dispatched by a toy like this!

523
00:27:24.160 --> 00:27:27.750
You're lucky, Zoro...
being born as a man.

524
00:27:27.750 --> 00:27:29.090
All I ever wanted was to be

525
00:27:29.090 --> 00:27:31.960
to be the world's greatest swordsman.

526
00:27:31.960 --> 00:27:33.880
Now promise me...

527
00:27:33.880 --> 00:27:38.550
Promise me that someday, one of us
will be the world's greatest swordsman.

528
00:27:38.550 --> 00:27:39.970
We'll see who gets there.

529
00:27:40.930 --> 00:27:41.930
[BOTH] It's a promise.

530
00:27:47.480 --> 00:27:49.940
[ZORO] To become the world's strongest!

531
00:27:51.190 --> 00:27:54.650
[ZORO growling]

532
00:27:54.650 --> 00:27:59.450
[ZORO grunting]

533
00:27:59.450 --> 00:28:01.700
[ZORO] I ask that you
let me have that sword.

534
00:28:01.700 --> 00:28:03.790
I'm gonna get stronger
than she ever was!

535
00:28:03.790 --> 00:28:06.830
Strong enough that my name
reaches up to the heavens!

536
00:28:06.830 --> 00:28:10.290
I am going to be the
world's greatest swordsman!

537
00:28:10.880 --> 00:28:14.090
I promised her... I promised...

538
00:28:19.590 --> 00:28:23.350
[ZORO grunting, panting]

539
00:28:23.350 --> 00:28:26.640
[ZORO] I will defeat this man... for her!

540
00:28:26.640 --> 00:28:31.440
[ZORO grunting]

541
00:28:31.440 --> 00:28:32.730
What is it then?

542
00:28:32.730 --> 00:28:35.490
What weight do you carry
upon your shoulders?

543
00:28:35.490 --> 00:28:37.280
Speak up, weakling!

544
00:28:37.280 --> 00:28:39.570
We're deeply impressed by your skills.

545
00:28:39.570 --> 00:28:41.370
Would you let us join you?

546
00:28:41.370 --> 00:28:43.740
We're the famed bounty hunting
duo that's fearsome enough

547
00:28:43.740 --> 00:28:47.160
to silence a crying child
by a hair: Yosaku and Johnny.

548
00:28:47.160 --> 00:28:49.170
How dare you call him "weakling"!

549
00:28:49.170 --> 00:28:50.420
You'll pay for that!

550
00:28:50.420 --> 00:28:52.090
We'll teach you a lesson!

551
00:28:52.090 --> 00:28:53.000
[YOSAKU, JOHNNY yell]

552
00:28:53.000 --> 00:28:53.710
[LUFFY] No!

553
00:28:53.710 --> 00:28:56.300
Yosaku! Johnny! Get back here!

554
00:28:56.300 --> 00:29:01.180
– Just stay put!
– [YOSAKU, JOHNNY growling]

555
00:29:01.180 --> 00:29:02.550
Luffy...

556
00:29:02.550 --> 00:29:05.640
[ZORO grunts]
No... I won't lose...

557
00:29:05.640 --> 00:29:07.730
I refuse to be defeated!

558
00:29:09.480 --> 00:29:15.480
[heartbeat thumps]

559
00:29:19.360 --> 00:29:19.950
Tiger...

560
00:29:19.950 --> 00:29:21.950
[LUFFY] World's greatest swordsman...

561
00:29:21.950 --> 00:29:24.030
Sounds pretty good!
The King of the Pirates

562
00:29:24.030 --> 00:29:26.540
wouldn't have any less
than the best on his crew.

563
00:29:26.540 --> 00:29:27.500
[ZORO] ... Trap!

564
00:29:48.600 --> 00:29:51.520
You are defeated, yet
you won't step back...

565
00:29:51.520 --> 00:29:53.730
Why not?

566
00:29:53.730 --> 00:29:56.650
But... I will not run...

567
00:29:56.650 --> 00:29:59.110
Even if I retreat a single step...

568
00:29:59.110 --> 00:30:01.740
I would be shattering
the promises I've made.

569
00:30:01.740 --> 00:30:03.410
I can't run...

570
00:30:03.410 --> 00:30:05.240
I would lose my honor.

571
00:30:05.240 --> 00:30:09.330
You see, without that, there
would be nothing left for me here.

572
00:30:10.330 --> 00:30:12.460
That's what defeat is.

573
00:30:12.460 --> 00:30:15.540
[ZORO chuckles]
Then I won't accept defeat.

574
00:30:16.340 --> 00:30:17.880
Then you'll die.

575
00:30:18.670 --> 00:30:20.920
I'd rather die than give up!

576
00:30:22.130 --> 00:30:24.010
[MIHAWK] A strong heart indeed!

577
00:30:24.010 --> 00:30:26.720
He chooses death before defeat!

578
00:30:26.720 --> 00:30:27.970
[ZORO grunts]

579
00:30:29.390 --> 00:30:31.770
Sir... State your name!

580
00:30:35.940 --> 00:30:38.650
I am... Roronoa Zoro!

581
00:30:38.650 --> 00:30:39.900
[MIHAWK] I'll remember it!

582
00:30:39.900 --> 00:30:43.450
No one as strong as you has
come around in quite some time.

583
00:30:44.860 --> 00:30:46.700
So as a swordsman's courtesy,

584
00:30:46.700 --> 00:30:50.580
I'll use the world's strongest
black sword to finish you.

585
00:30:50.580 --> 00:30:53.330
Thank you... I appreciate it.

586
00:30:54.000 --> 00:30:55.540
[PIRATE A] Look! He took it out!

587
00:30:55.540 --> 00:30:58.670
[PIRATE B] That's the sword
that sliced up the ship!

588
00:30:58.670 --> 00:31:00.340
[ZORO] So this is it...

589
00:31:00.340 --> 00:31:03.130
Will it be the world's
strongest... or death?

590
00:31:07.680 --> 00:31:08.430
[LUFFY growls]

591
00:31:08.430 --> 00:31:10.180
Enough, Big Bro! Stop it! Please!

592
00:31:10.180 --> 00:31:12.770
[ZORO] Three-Sword Style Secret Technique!

593
00:31:15.650 --> 00:31:16.560
[MIHAWK] Fall!

594
00:31:16.560 --> 00:31:18.230
[ZORO] Three Thousand Worlds!

595
00:31:26.110 --> 00:31:27.620
[ZORO] I've lost...

596
00:31:29.120 --> 00:31:32.290
[ZORO] Never in my life
did I imagine I'd lose.

597
00:31:34.080 --> 00:31:37.210
[ZORO] So this is the power
of the greatest in the world.

598
00:31:40.750 --> 00:31:41.670
But why...?

599
00:31:43.050 --> 00:31:46.010
Scars on the back are
a swordsman's shame.

600
00:31:46.010 --> 00:31:46.970
Fine.

601
00:31:50.600 --> 00:31:56.100
Zoro!

602
00:31:58.190 --> 00:32:01.610
[MIHAWK] You shouldn't rush
these things, young man.

603
00:32:02.440 --> 00:32:04.240
[USOPP] Zoro!

604
00:32:05.110 --> 00:32:06.740
[YOSAKU, JOHNNY] Big Bro!

605
00:32:07.280 --> 00:32:09.570
No!

606
00:32:09.570 --> 00:32:11.080
[SANJI] Why?!

607
00:32:13.240 --> 00:32:16.910
[ZORO] I devoted my entire life to becoming
the world's greatest swordsman...

608
00:32:16.910 --> 00:32:20.210
It was my choice, so I'm the only
one who gets to call me stupid.

609
00:32:22.000 --> 00:32:23.500
[SANJI] He's insane!

610
00:32:23.500 --> 00:32:26.170
His opponent was way out of his league!

611
00:32:26.170 --> 00:32:28.470
How this fight would end
was clear from the start!

612
00:32:28.470 --> 00:32:29.930
Why choose death?!

613
00:32:29.930 --> 00:32:31.510
Don't be stupid!

614
00:32:31.510 --> 00:32:33.470
Give up your ambition and live!

615
00:32:36.640 --> 00:32:41.110
So this is the power of the
Grand Line; it's terrifying!

616
00:32:41.110 --> 00:32:44.820
The Pirate Hunter Zoro was as
helpless as a newborn baby!

617
00:32:44.820 --> 00:32:45.940
[LUFFY] Damn you...

618
00:32:48.740 --> 00:32:49.740
[YOSAKU, JOHNNY] Big bro!

619
00:32:51.910 --> 00:32:55.700
[LUFFY yells]

620
00:32:55.700 --> 00:32:57.830
He must be some kind of freak!

621
00:32:57.830 --> 00:32:59.120
[SANJI gasps]

622
00:32:59.120 --> 00:33:03.340
So that loudmouthed little twerp
has the power of a devil fruit.

623
00:33:03.340 --> 00:33:04.880
[LUFFY] Bastard!

624
00:33:06.510 --> 00:33:09.380
[MIHAWK] Are you
that young warrior's comrade?

625
00:33:09.380 --> 00:33:12.470
I'm impressed with you
for not interfering.

626
00:33:14.180 --> 00:33:16.600
[LUFFY grunts]

627
00:33:16.600 --> 00:33:18.770
[MIHAWK] There's nothing
to be upset about.

628
00:33:18.770 --> 00:33:20.230
Your friend will live.

629
00:33:20.230 --> 00:33:21.230
[LUFFY] Huh?

630
00:33:21.230 --> 00:33:23.690
[YOSAKU] Big Bro! Say something, please!

631
00:33:23.690 --> 00:33:25.900
[LUFFY] Zoro!

632
00:33:25.900 --> 00:33:26.860
[ZORO groans]

633
00:33:26.860 --> 00:33:27.740
[LUFFY] Zoro!

634
00:33:27.740 --> 00:33:29.950
C'mon, let's hurry up and
get him out of the water.

635
00:33:31.660 --> 00:33:33.820
[USOPP] I've got some medicine! Here!

636
00:33:33.820 --> 00:33:36.580
It's still far too
early for you to die.

637
00:33:36.580 --> 00:33:39.910
My name is Hawk-Eye Mihawk!

638
00:33:39.910 --> 00:33:42.960
You're strong but there
is much for you to learn.

639
00:33:42.960 --> 00:33:46.000
No matter how many years it
takes, I will hold this title as

640
00:33:46.000 --> 00:33:48.670
the greatest in the world,
and wait for you!

641
00:33:48.670 --> 00:33:51.970
Until that day, you
must hone your skills!

642
00:33:51.970 --> 00:33:55.430
Then... seek me out! Roronoa Zoro!

643
00:33:56.890 --> 00:33:58.140
[YOSAKU] Please say something!

644
00:33:58.140 --> 00:33:59.640
[YOSAKU, JOHNNY] Anything!

645
00:34:00.430 --> 00:34:04.150
Not just anyone can earn
the regard of Hawk-Eye Mihawk.

646
00:34:05.400 --> 00:34:06.520
[MIHAWK] You...

647
00:34:06.520 --> 00:34:08.360
What is your goal?

648
00:34:08.360 --> 00:34:10.240
To be the King!

649
00:34:10.240 --> 00:34:13.070
Your ambitions are even
loftier than your friend's.

650
00:34:13.070 --> 00:34:14.280
That's quite a task.

651
00:34:14.280 --> 00:34:17.030
Yeah, well, you just let
me worry about that.

652
00:34:17.030 --> 00:34:18.450
Bleh!

653
00:34:18.450 --> 00:34:20.120
[USOPP] He's alive!

654
00:34:20.120 --> 00:34:21.790
He was just unconscious!

655
00:34:21.790 --> 00:34:22.540
Big Bro!

656
00:34:22.540 --> 00:34:25.330
If you're alive, then say something!

657
00:34:25.330 --> 00:34:26.250
[gasps] Zoro!

658
00:34:26.250 --> 00:34:27.090
[YOSAKU] Big Bro!

659
00:34:29.090 --> 00:34:30.720
[ZORO] Luffy...

660
00:34:31.380 --> 00:34:32.260
Can you hear me...?

661
00:34:32.260 --> 00:34:33.130
[LUFFY] Yeah!

662
00:34:35.600 --> 00:34:37.560
I'm sorry for disappointing you.

663
00:34:37.560 --> 00:34:41.680
I know that you need nothing less than
the greatest swordsman in the world...

664
00:34:41.680 --> 00:34:43.690
I've let you down...

665
00:34:43.690 --> 00:34:45.150
Please forgive me.

666
00:34:47.690 --> 00:34:50.280
Okay, okay! You can
stop saying things now!

667
00:34:50.280 --> 00:34:52.610
[ZORO] I solemnly swear...

668
00:34:52.610 --> 00:34:54.360
From this moment forward...

669
00:34:54.360 --> 00:34:57.030
That I will never lose again!

670
00:34:57.030 --> 00:34:59.450
[ZORO chokes]

671
00:34:59.450 --> 00:35:04.540
Until the day comes... when
I defeat him and take his title...

672
00:35:04.540 --> 00:35:08.040
I will never... never be defeated!

673
00:35:08.040 --> 00:35:12.470
Is that okay... King of the Pirates?!

674
00:35:15.180 --> 00:35:18.140
[LUFFY laughs] Yup!

675
00:35:18.140 --> 00:35:19.930
You're a good team.

676
00:35:19.930 --> 00:35:21.930
I hope to see you again... someday.

677
00:35:23.850 --> 00:35:25.980
[KRIEG] Hey! Hawk-Eye!

678
00:35:25.980 --> 00:35:29.900
I was under the impression that
you had come here to take my life.

679
00:35:29.900 --> 00:35:33.860
Weren't you here to kill Don
Krieg, ruler of the East Blue?

680
00:35:33.860 --> 00:35:35.990
The thought had crossed my mind...

681
00:35:35.990 --> 00:35:39.780
But I've had enough fun for today,
so I'm going home to get some rest.

682
00:35:39.780 --> 00:35:41.620
I don't care if you've had enough.

683
00:35:41.620 --> 00:35:43.500
I haven't even gotten started.

684
00:35:43.500 --> 00:35:44.710
Um, but, sir...

685
00:35:44.710 --> 00:35:47.750
Maybe it's not a good idea
to try to keep him here!

686
00:35:47.750 --> 00:35:50.800
Now it's time to die!

687
00:35:50.800 --> 00:35:53.130
[MIHAWK] He just won't learn, will he?

688
00:35:55.470 --> 00:35:59.550
[PIRATES screaming]

689
00:36:01.140 --> 00:36:03.640
Aw, damn... He escaped.

690
00:36:03.640 --> 00:36:04.680
[LUFFY grunts]

691
00:36:04.680 --> 00:36:06.390
[COOKS scream]

692
00:36:12.020 --> 00:36:13.690
[LUFFY] Usopp!

693
00:36:13.690 --> 00:36:14.690
Luffy!

694
00:36:14.690 --> 00:36:16.070
Go on ahead!

695
00:36:16.070 --> 00:36:17.910
I'll leave Nami to you!

696
00:36:17.910 --> 00:36:18.660
[USOPP] Roger that!

697
00:36:18.660 --> 00:36:20.070
Don't you worry about a thing!

698
00:36:20.070 --> 00:36:21.990
Zoro and I are gonna
get her right back!

699
00:36:21.990 --> 00:36:24.620
And make sure you get that
cook to join our crew!

700
00:36:24.620 --> 00:36:29.920
And then... on the Going Merry,
the five of us'll set sail... to the Grand Line!

701
00:36:29.920 --> 00:36:32.170
[LUFFY laughs]
Yeah! Let's do it!

702
00:36:32.170 --> 00:36:33.170
[KRIEG] All right, men!

703
00:36:33.170 --> 00:36:37.340
We ran into a little distraction from
our plan, but the real fight starts now!

704
00:36:37.340 --> 00:36:39.010
We're gonna take that ship!

705
00:36:39.010 --> 00:36:40.140
[PIRATES] Yes, sir!

706
00:36:40.140 --> 00:36:44.850
[LUFFY] Hey, Pops, can I stop doing these
chores if I get those pirates outta here?

707
